; mirror-census-run.fk — ask the body which of each native's mirrors still stand.
;
; preflight-exec: forbidden
; preludes: form/form-stdlib/mirror-glass.bml
;
; The bearing census answers WHICH DOOR IS NEXT. This one answers whether a door
; is REACHABLE — and the two questions are not the same question. A cost lens
; weighs each door and sees weight, never reach; on 2026-09-08 it named a wall
; where a complete native had been standing since before it was named, and the
; remedy it asked for was to mint what already existed (corpus row 1358,
; limbkept). This door is the reading that would have said so.
;
; It touches nothing. Nine files are read, no state is written, and the frame is
; held open so a taker can read it:
;
;     ./fkwu observe/mirror-census-run.fk &
;     ./fkwu observe/mirror-census-take.fk
;
; To read a tree this process is not running in — an older checkout, a sibling's
; worktree — put its root on one line in /tmp/mirror-census-root. That is not a
; convenience. `str_find` is one of the natives this census searches with, so on
; the tree that had lost its row the census CANNOT RUN THERE AT ALL: the wound
; disables the tool that finds it. A body cannot always read a wound with the
; body that has it; it can read the text with a body that is well.
;
;     echo /tmp/pre-restoration-worktree > /tmp/mirror-census-root
;     ./fkwu observe/mirror-census-run.fk
;
; Read the panel worst-first. An armhush is a native standing with no route, and
; the recipe the body walks instead is being paid for every call. A seedgap is
; the reading that says GO LOOK: three sibling kernels hold the meaning, the seed
; holds no route to it, and the arms-nobody-names list at the foot of the panel
; is where its arm will be if it has one.

(do
    (defn mcr-root-path () "/tmp/mirror-census-root")
    ; a root file that is not there is not an error; it means this tree, and the
    ; census says which tree it read rather than leaving the reader to assume
    (defn mcr-trim-nl (s)
        (if (eq (str_len s) 0) s
            (if (eq (str_byte_at s (sub (str_len s) 1)) 10)
                (mcr-trim-nl (substring s 0 (sub (str_len s) 1)))
                s)))
    (defn mcr-root ()
        (if (lt (file_size (mcr-root-path)) 0) ""
            (mcr-trim-nl (read_file (mcr-root-path)))))
    (defn mcr-hold-ms () 20000)

    (let root (mcr-root))
    (let where (print (str_concat "  reading the tree at: " (if (eq (str_len root) 0) "this checkout" root))))
    (let t0 (now_unix_ms))
    (let worst (mgl-witness root t0))
    (let held (host_sleep_ms (mcr-hold-ms)))
    worst)
